    "faq": {
      "type": "faq-schema",
      "blocks": {
        "q1": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the difference between Crib 5 and Crib 7?",
            "answer": "<p>Crib 5 and Crib 7 are flammability ratings from the BS 5852 ignition-source test. The higher the crib number, the more severe the ignition source the fabric resists. Crib 5 covers severe-hazard contract environments; Crib 7 covers the highest-hazard applications. In our range, the Crib 5 grade (Portus) carries Crib 5 and the Crib 7 / B1 grade (Prosoft) carries Crib 7.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What does B1 certification mean?",
            "answer": "<p>B1 is a flame-retardancy classification under the German standard DIN 4102-1. A B1-rated material is classed as flame-retardant (not easily ignitable) and is widely specified for public buildings and transport interiors. In our range, the Crib 7 / B1 grade (Prosoft) holds DIN 4102-1 B1.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can these fabrics be cleaned with bleach and alcohol?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. The coated surface is engineered to withstand diluted sodium-hypochlorite (bleach) solutions and alcohol-based disinfectants used in clinical and public-hygiene cleaning protocols, without cracking or losing colour. Avoid abrasive pads and undiluted solvents.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are Monteiro Performance Fabrics PFAS-free?",
            "answer": "<p>Where stated, our fabrics are free of intentionally-added PFAS. [TO CONFIRM which lines carry a PFAS-free declaration and the basis for it.]</p>"
          }
        },
        "q5": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What Martindale abrasion rating do the fabrics achieve?",
            "answer": "<p>Abrasion resistance is measured in Martindale rubs under ISO 5470-2, the coated-fabric method. Our performance grades reach 400,000 Martindale rubs — contract / heavy-duty grade.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q6": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I get the certificates and test reports for a project?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Tell us the application and the standards your specification calls for, and our technical team will supply the relevant certificates, test reports and samples.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
